# Line endings of every checkout, on Windows or Linux and whatever core.autocrlf says. The prompt's texts are string
# literals inside the DLLs, and the widget's CSS and JavaScript ship as files in the packages: the line endings of the
# sources end up in the published bytes. 1.0.0 was built from CRLF sources, so every text file is checked out CRLF.
# The repository itself keeps LF.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Scripts with a shebang stay LF: run directly on Linux, a CRLF first line asks for "python3\r".
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Binary files, named rather than guessed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary
*.snupkg binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.snk binary
*.pfx binary
